      "content": "thanks for this. it's a good start but honestly it feels a little thin. the auditors are really going to nitpick if they see entire sections summarized in just a few bullet points. \n\nthey want to see a \"granular breakdown\" where every single nuance of the regulation is given its own dedicated heading. like, don't just group \"Level 1 assets\"—i want a heading for the reserves, then a heading for the securities, etc. \n\ncan you expand this? make it way more detailed by creating much more specific sub-headings. even if a section is only one or two sentences long, give it its own heading to ensure the structural density score stays high. we really need to maximize that heading count so they don't think we're skipping over the fine print.",
